[[File:Jedi_shuttlebus.png|thumb|right|275px|A speeder bus on Coruscant]]
A '''speeder bus''', '''hoverbus''' or simply '''bus''' was a large [[repulsorlift]] vehicle used for group transportation. The [[AppSci SaberCats]] of the [[Junior Academy of Applied Sciences]] on [[Lothal]] used a speeder bus for traveling to [[grav-ball]] matches.<ref name="EotG">''[[Servants of the Empire: Edge of the Galaxy]]''</ref>

[[GoCorp]] manufactured the [[Util-313]] speeder bus, an eighteen-[[meter]]-long [[Atmosphere|air]] [[transport]] designed for traversing through [[City|cities]] that was used by [[Galactic Republic]] [[senator]]s, high-ranking [[Republic Military|military]] personnel, and the [[Jedi Order]]. With gullwing doors on either side, the shuttle bus was also surrounded by [[transparisteel]] windows, allowing passengers a 360-degree view. As a result of the GoCorp airbus being unarmed, the [[Galactic Senate]] deployed fighter escorts for buses that carried high-ranking officials on [[Coruscant]] to ensure their safety.<ref name="ESOV">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref>

[[Standard year|Years]] before the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Okadiah Garson]], an inhabitant of the [[planet]] [[Gorse]], owned a [[Mark Six Smoothride]] hoverbus, which he allowed his friend, [[Kanan Jarrus]] to use to carry passengers from the [[Moonglow Polychemical|Moonglow]] facilities to the bars in the area of Gorse known as [[the Pits]].<ref name="AND" />

Cadets hoping to enroll in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Academy|Imperial Academies]] often arrived at their planet's academy via hoverbus.<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref>

